/*!
    \page profiler-select-event-ranges.html
    \previouspage creator-how-tos.html

    \ingroup creator-how-to-profile
    \ingroup profiler-analyze-data

    \title Select event ranges

    Select an event range in \uicontrol Timeline to view the time it represents
    or to zoom into a specific region of the trace. For QML events, you can view
    the frame rate of events and compare them with the frame rate of similar
    events.

    To activate the selection tool:

    \list 1
        \li Select \uicontrol {Select Range}.
        \li Click in the timeline to set the beginning of the event range.
        \li Drag the selection handle to define the end of the range.
    \endlist

    Use event ranges also to measure delays between two subsequent
    events. Place a range between the end of the first event and the beginning
    of the second event. \uicontrol Duration shows the delay
    between the events in milliseconds.

    To narrow down the current range in the timeline view,
    \uicontrol Statistics, and \uicontrol {Flame Graph} views, right-click
    the range and select \uicontrol {Analyze Current Range}. To return to
    the full range, select \uicontrol {Analyze Full Range} in the context menu.

    \section1 Zoom into event ranges

    To zoom into an event range, double-click it.

    \section1 Remove event ranges

    To remove an event range, close the \uicontrol Selection dialog.

    \if defined(qtcreator)
    \sa {Profile}{How to: Profile}, {Profilers}, {Profiling applications},
    {Performance Analyzer}

    \endif
*/
